// =============================================================================
// SaaS platform Prisma fragment: MaintenanceWindow
// =============================================================================
//
// REFERENCE SNIPPET — see 01-subscription.prisma for conventions.
//
// One row per maintenance window: announced to the tenants ahead of time,
// locked while a deploy runs a migration that must not race with requests, and
// ended when the operator says so. A window can also be locked at once without
// having been announced, which leaves `startsAt` null.
//
// While a window is locked, every running version of the application reads this
// table on its requests — the one being replaced as well as the one replacing
// it. Its shape is therefore part of the contract between two releases: it
// gains columns, and never in a deploy the lock protects.
//
// At most ONE window is open (not yet ended) at a time. Prisma cannot express a
// partial unique index; the one that holds it is in
// sql/constraints.postgres.sql, and it is what makes two operators locking at
// the same moment land one window rather than two.
//
// Optional: adopt it where `maintenance` is turned on in
// `SaaSiCatModule.forRoot`, which refuses to start without a place to keep
// windows.

model MaintenanceWindow {
    id        String    @id @default(uuid())
    // What the tenants were told: the announced start and the expected end.
    // Neither starts or ends the lock — that is the operator's command.
    startsAt  DateTime?
    endsAt    DateTime?
    // The operator's words to the tenants, shown as written.
    message   String?
    // When the window was recorded — announced, or locked at once — and by whom
    // (an actor tag, as the audit log writes it).
    createdAt DateTime  @default(now())
    createdBy String
    // Null while the window is only announced.
    lockedAt  DateTime?
    lockedBy  String?
    // Set when the window is over: unlocked, or cancelled before it locked.
    endedAt   DateTime?
    endedBy   String?

    @@index([createdAt])
    @@map("maintenance_windows")
}
